{% block title %}AC11.03 – LAN Design and VLAN Segmentation{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <div class="container">

        <h1>AC11.03 – Designing a LAN and Segmenting with VLANs</h1>
        <p><strong>Objective:</strong> Design a functional Local Area Network (LAN) and segment the network using VLANs to improve organization and security.</p>

        <hr>

        <h2>Reflective Analysis</h2>
        <p>
            In the SAE21 project, I designed and configured a multi-site network with VLAN segmentation
            (admin, services, training_A, training_B, teachers). I also created a VLSM addressing plan
            based on the 172.16.0.0/16 network while respecting the constraints of each LAN.
            This activity helped me understand the importance of logical structuring and segmentation
            for network performance and security.
        </p>

        <h2>Evidence Documents</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>VLSM addressing plan.</li>
            <li>Packet Tracer VLAN configuration.</li>
            <li>Multi-site network diagram.</li>
            <li>Inter-VLAN connectivity tests.</li>
        </ul>

